Let lookup() move on from a binding it could not append as a branch.

After the first valid binding has become the Request-URI, lookup() appends
every other valid binding of the IMPU as a branch, in a while loop that
advances at the bottom of its body:

	while(impucontact) {
		ptr = impucontact->contact;
		if(VALID_CONTACT(...)) {
			if(... get_path_dst_uri(&ptr->path, &path_dst) < 0)
				continue;
			if(km_append_branch(...) == -1)
				continue;   /* "Also give a chance to the next branches" */
		}
		impucontact = impucontact->next;
	}

Both continues jump past that advance, so the loop re-examines the same
binding, fails the same way, and never terminates - with the udomain lock
lookup() took for the IMPU still held, so every later request that hashes to
that slot blocks behind it too. The comment says what was meant: skip this
binding, try the rest.

km_append_branch() fails deterministically once the transaction has
max_branches destinations (12 by default, which serving.cfg does not raise),
so the thirteenth valid binding of one IMPU is enough: the first becomes the
Request-URI, the next eleven are appended, the twelfth append fails, and the
worker spins. One REGISTER can bind that many - it may carry any number of
Contacts, and route[REBIND] only retires bindings from earlier
registrations, not siblings in the same one - after which the first
terminating request to that identity takes a worker down with it. A Path
that get_path_dst_uri() cannot parse does the same on any binding.

Turned into a for loop, so the advance runs on continue too. Nothing else
changes: a failed binding is still skipped with its error logged, and the
bindings after it are still tried.

diff --git a/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/lookup.c b/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/lookup.c
--- a/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/lookup.c
+++ b/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/lookup.c
@@ -216,9 +216,13 @@
 		goto done;
 
 	//the last i was the first valid contact we found - let's go through the rest of valid contacts and append the branches.
+	//
+	//A for, not a while: both failure paths below skip to the next contact
+	//with `continue`, and in a while that skips the advance at the bottom of
+	//the body too - the same contact is retried forever, udomain lock held.
 	if(impucontact)
 		impucontact = impucontact->next;
-	while(impucontact) {
+	for(; impucontact; impucontact = impucontact->next) {
 		ptr = impucontact->contact;
 		if(VALID_UE_TYPE(ptr, ue_type) && VALID_CONTACT(ptr, act_time)
 				&& allowed_method(_m, ptr)) {
@@ -240,7 +244,6 @@
 				continue;
 			}
 		}
-		impucontact = impucontact->next;
 	}
 
 done:
